<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC QUOTA WATCHDOG COMMITTEE ENDS SESSION.</title>
<headline>OPEC QUOTA WATCHDOG COMMITTEE ENDS SESSION.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC's quota watchdog committee ended brief discussions on Tuesday with Iran's Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh repeating his call for compliance to official output quotas.</p>
<p>&quot;Even one barrel of violation is very bad,&quot; Aghazadeh told reporters.</p>
<p>He said the issue would be discussed at the full ministerial conference which gets underway at 1400 GMT on Wednesday. Nigeria's Dan Etete said it was not accepted by all OPEC members that output was beyond official limits. Nigeria, allegedly, is one of OPEC's largest quota violators.</p>
<p>Etete noted the big gap between official member country submissions on output and secondary media estimates.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
